  "gaps": [
    "The program table prints only a combined 'Remaining General Education and Elective Courses 45'. The 19 elective credits are derived arithmetic, not a printed figure: 45 minus 26 remaining general education credits.",
    "The 26 remaining general education credits are an inference. They assume the business core covers four areas: WRTG 112 (communications), STAT 200 (mathematics, 3), ECON 201/203 (behavioral and social sciences, 6), and HMGT 305 (computing/IT, 3). The capture states that these 15 business core credits 'may be applied to general education requirements', and the course sequencing table maps them to those areas. The capture gives no explicit remaining-gen-ed figure.",
    "The capture never labels its credit units as semester hours. 'Semester' is assumed for the UMGC undergraduate catalog.",
    "Residency policies are not tied to specific courses, so no requirement is flagged institutionalOnly. The policies are: at least 30 credits (normally the final 30) completed at UMGC; half the required major credits completed at UMGC; at least 15 upper-level credits (300–499) completed at UMGC.",
    "Other policies not encoded per course: at least half of major credits must be graded coursework; minimum grade of C in any course applied to the major; minimum 2.0 GPA; pass/fail allowed only for electives (max 18 credits); WRTG 112 must be completed with C- or better within the first 24 credits.",
    "Course prerequisites and course descriptions are not included in the capture.",
    "The catalog requirements apply to students who begin continuous enrollment on or after August 1, 2026. The catalog year is taken from the page footer/URL ('2026–2027')."
  ],
